-- count so far was taken under a list of operations chosen by hand, with the choice justified in a
-- comment: these are proper, that one is a reflection, this one no medium supplies. The justification
-- belongs in the construction. An operation is admitted by an observation when two things hold: the
-- process that performs it runs faster than the observation resolves, and either it is a proper motion
-- or the medium cannot tell the molecule from its mirror image. Both conditions are facts about the
-- observation and the process, not about the molecule, so the group is a function of the pair.
--
-- a process: the permutation it performs, the order of magnitude of its rate in inverse seconds, and
-- whether it is a proper motion. A methyl rotation is proper and fast. A ring flip is proper and its rate
-- depends on the temperature. The exchange of two groups across a mirror plane is not a process at all in
-- this sense -- nothing performs it -- and it is recorded as improper, which an achiral medium supplies
-- and a chiral one does not.
Proc : Type 0
Proc = (p : Nat → Nat) × ((r : Nat) × Bool)
